class:: StereoBalance
summary:: Relative left and right channel energy
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Amplitude

description::
Computes (sum(R.squared) - sum(L.squared)) / (sum(R.squared) + sum(L.squared)). Negative means left, positive means right.

Uses an exact rolling sample window, with output held at zero until it is full. The update cost is linear in the input block size, with a once-per-window sum rebase to bound roundoff drift. Memory is two windows of doubles, allocated at initialization. Formulas are independently implemented from energy, M/S decomposition, and Pearson correlation. Silence returns zero.

Vanilla Amplitude can track channel levels separately; this UGen directly relates the channels over a fixed shared interval.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time rolling window, 0.001..2 seconds; default 0.05.

returns::
Signed balance from -1 (left only) to +1 (right only).

examples::
StereoBalance measures instantaneous energy balance between left and right channels (-1 for left only, +1 for right only). In this example, it monitors a dynamic stereo mix: when one channel becomes heavily dominant, an active differential amplifier applies gentle compensating inverse gain, keeping the center image stable without flattening stereo width. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.stereo:: displays the stereo balance needle and width.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("stereo.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 3);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.isKindOf(Buffer) and: { ~miraBuffer.numChannels >= 2 }) {
            PlayBuf.ar(2, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
                var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1);
                [sig, DelayC.ar(sig, 0.02, 0.003)]
            } {
                // Synthetic stereo fallback
                var l = Saw.ar(220) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                var r = Saw.ar(222) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                [l, r]
            }
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);

        var balance = StereoBalance.kr(source[0], source[1], windowTime: 0.05);
        var balLag = balance.lag(0.08);
        var compL = (1 - (balLag * 0.5)).clip(0.5, 1.5);
        var compR = (1 + (balLag * 0.5)).clip(0.5, 1.5);
        var centered = [source[0] * compL, source[1] * compR] * 0.25;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, [balLag, 1.0, 1.0]) };
        centered * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.stereo("Stereo Balance", ~miraBus);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
